<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Long Recess</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1529">1529</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Langer Rezess</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Long Recess (Langer Rezess) of 1529 was an agreement between the council and citizens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> concluded with the introduction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. It gave the propertied citizens, organised by parish, a share in government beside the council, including a say over taxation and church affairs. It remained a basis of the city's constitution for centuries.</p></div>
